updated to include the specific problem ID. Conversely, closing the modal triggers a hash reset back to a default state. A copyable route, containing the problem ID, will also be rendered within the modal header.\n\nA click on the copy button generates the complete URL, incorporating the current domain, path, and the problem-specific hash. This allows the user to copy a direct link to the problem. The copied link will have feedback to confirm for the user.\n\n\nThe code generates a URL route for a problem ID and attempts to copy it to the clipboard.  A fallback mechanism handles cases where the clipboard API is unavailable, which will show feedback to the user on success.\n\nThe code defines an import function with options to handle duplicate problems; it validates the input and prepares various lookup maps for duplicate detection. The function normalizes problem titles and URLs to ensure consistent comparison.\n\n\nDuplicate problem entries are being checked during import, using multiple criteria: ID, LeetCode number, normalized title, and normalized source URL. The existing data is compared against the new entries, reporting any duplicates found. If a duplicate is found, the relevant information is logged.\n\n\nThe code updates problem records if they exist, otherwise it creates new ones, assigning new IDs. It handles cases where an ID is missing or already exists, generating a new, unique ID. The function validates the data, assigning defaults and normalizing certain fields like the title and source URL. Duplicate detection logic will be used when importing data.\n\n\nThe code validates the imported problem records and assigns default values for missing data, normalizing fields like titles and URLs for consistent matching. It uses multiple lookup maps for efficient duplicate detection based on ID, LeetCode number, normalized title, and normalized source URL. After validating and deduplicating, it updates existing records or creates new ones, assigning unique IDs where necessary. The import process also tracks the number of imported problems.\n\n\nAn import modal will be added, featuring a textarea for JSON input and an \"Analyze/Preview\" button displaying import statistics. This modal also incorporates an \"Import Now\" button, triggering the import process and displaying a confirmation message upon completion.\n\nCSS classes are being reviewed, and a script to systematically apply these styles to the application's stylesheet is planned. The script will target specific UI elements based on the defined class names.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# scratch/update_dsa_dashboard_phase4.py\n# Updates dsa_dashboard.js for Phase 4:\n# - Review status in progress & methods (isReview, toggleReview, markReview, unmarkReview)\n# - Sorting: order_asc, order_desc, title_asc, title_desc, diff_asc, diff_desc, lc_asc, lc_desc\n# - Filtering: topic, difficulty, status (not_started, attempted, solved, review, bookmarked, with_notes), pattern, onlyBookmarked\n# - Pagination & page size control (10, 25, 50, 100, all) with First/Last/Prev/Next/Ellipsis\n# - URL hash router (#dsa/problem/:id) and unique route sharing\n# - Import engine with multi-criteria duplicate prevention (ID, LC#, Title, URL)\n\nimport os\n\nwith open('app_build/dsa_dashboard.js', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    code = f.read()\n\n# 1. Update loadProgress to include review array\ntarget_load_progress = \"\"\"          return {\n            solved: Array.isArray(parsed.solved) ? parsed.solved : [],\n            attempted: Array.isArray(parsed.attempted) ? parsed.attempted : [],\n            bookmarked: Array.isArray(parsed.bookmarked) ? parsed.bookmarked : [],\n            history: Array.isArray(parsed.history) ? parsed.history : [],\n            notes: (parsed.notes && typeof parsed.notes === 'object') ? parsed.notes : {},\n            lastPracticedId: parsed.lastPracticedId || null\n          };\"\"\"\n\nreplacement_load_progress = \"\"\"          return {\n            solved: Array.isArray(parsed.solved) ? parsed.solved : [],\n            attempted: Array.isArray(parsed.attempted) ? parsed.attempted : [],\n            review: Array.isArray(parsed.review) ? parsed.review : [],\n            bookmarked: Array.isArray(parsed.bookmarked) ? parsed.bookmarked : [],\n            history: Array.isArray(parsed.history) ? parsed.history : [],\n            notes: (parsed.notes && typeof parsed.notes === 'object') ? parsed.notes : {},\n            lastPracticedId: parsed.lastPracticedId || null\n          };\"\"\"\n\nassert target_load_progress in code, \"target_load_progress not found\"\ncode = code.replace(target_load_progress, replacement_load_progress, 1)\n\ntarget_fallback_progress = \"\"\"      return {\n        solved: [],\n        attempted: [],\n        bookmarked: [],\n        history: [],\n        notes: {},\n        lastPracticedId: null\n      };\"\"\"\n\nreplacement_fallback_progress = \"\"\"      return {\n        solved: [],\n        attempted: [],\n        review: [],\n        bookmarked: [],\n        history: [],\n        notes: {},\n        lastPracticedId: null\n      };\"\"\"\n\nassert target_fallback_progress in code, \"target_fallback_progress not found\"\ncode = code.replace(target_fallback_progress, replacement_fallback_progress, 1)\n\nprint(\"Progress data structure updated successfully\")\n","Description":"Test replacement 1 for dsa_dashboard.js","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef\\scratch\\update_dsa_dashboard_phase4.py","toolAction":"Creating update_dsa_dashboard_phase4.py","toolSummary":"Create phase 4 update script"}}]}
