{"step_index":2097,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:54:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-27T13:24:55+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-27T13:24:55+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js`\nTotal Lines: 2290\nTotal Bytes: 101371\nShowing lines 1770 to 1840\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1770:       `;\r\n1771:     }\r\n1772: \r\n1773:     renderProblemTableOnly() {\r\n1774:       const container = document.getElementById('dsaProblemTableContainer');\r\n1775:       if (container) {\r\n1776:         const topicOverride = this.currentSubTab === 'topic_detail' ? this.activeTopicDetail : null;\r\n1777:         container.innerHTML = this.renderProblemTableContent(topicOverride);\r\n1778:       }\r\n1779:     }\r\n1780: \r\n1781:     getFilteredProblems(overrideTopic = null) {\r\n1782:       let list = this.problems.slice();\r\n1783:       const activeTopic = overrideTopic || this.selectedTopic;\r\n1784: \r\n1785:       // Search query\r\n1786:       if (this.searchQuery) {\r\n1787:         const q = this.searchQuery;\r\n1788:         list = list.filter(p => {\r\n1789:           const matchTitle = p.title.toLowerCase().includes(q);\r\n1790:           const matchNum = String(p.leetcodeNumber).includes(q);\r\n1791:           const matchPattern = p.pattern.toLowerCase().includes(q);\r\n1792:           const matchDesc = p.description.toLowerCase().includes(q);\r\n1793:           const matchTopic = (p.topics && p.topics.some(t => t.toLowerCase().includes(q))) || (p.topic && p.topic.toLowerCase().includes(q));\r\n1794:           return matchTitle || matchNum || matchPattern || matchDesc || matchTopic;\r\n1795:         });\r\n1796:       }\r\n1797: \r\n1798:       // Topic filter (multi-topic matching!)\r\n1799:       if (activeTopic && activeTopic !== 'all') {\r\n1800:         list = list.filter(p => (p.topics && p.topics.includes(activeTopic)) || p.topic === activeTopic);\r\n1801:       }\r\n1802: \r\n1803:       // Algorithmic Pattern filter\r\n1804:       if (this.selectedPattern && this.selectedPattern !== 'all') {\r\n1805:         list = list.filter(p => p.pattern === this.selectedPattern);\r\n1806:       }\r\n1807: \r\n1808:       // Difficulty filter\r\n1809:       if (this.selectedDifficulty && this.selectedDifficulty !== 'all') {\r\n1810:         list = list.filter(p => p.difficulty === this.selectedDifficulty);\r\n1811:       }\r\n1812: \r\n1813:       // Status filter\r\n1814:       if (this.selectedStatus && this.selectedStatus !== 'all') {\r\n1815:         if (this.selectedStatus === 'solved') {\r\n1816:           list = list.filter(p => this.progress.solved.includes(p.id));\r\n1817:         } else if (this.selectedStatus === 'attempted') {\r\n1818:           list = list.filter(p => this.progress.attempted.includes(p.id) && !this.progress.solved.includes(p.id));\r\n1819:         } else if (this.selectedStatus === 'not_started') {\r\n1820:           list = list.filter(p => !this.progress.solved.includes(p.id) && !this.progress.attempted.includes(p.id));\r\n1821:         } else if (this.selectedStatus === 'bookmarked') {\r\n1822:           list = list.filter(p => this.progress.bookmarked.includes(p.id));\r\n1823:         } else if (this.selectedStatus === 'with_notes') {\r\n1824:           list = list.filter(p => this.hasNote(p.id));\r\n1825:         }\r\n1826:       }\r\n1827: \r\n1828:       // Sorting\r\n1829:       const diffRank = { Easy: 1, Medium: 2, Hard: 3 };\r\n1830:       if (this.selectedSort === 'lc_asc') {\r\n1831:         list.sort((a, b) => a.leetcodeNumber - b.leetcodeNumber);\r\n1832:       } else if (this.selectedSort === 'lc_desc') {\r\n1833:         list.sort((a, b) => b.leetcodeNumber - a.leetcodeNumber);\r\n1834:       } else if (this.selectedSort === 'diff_asc') {\r\n1835:         list.sort((a, b) => (diffRank[a.difficulty] || 0) - (diffRank[b.difficulty] || 0));\r\n1836:       } else if (this.selectedSort === 'title_asc') {\r\n1837:         list.sort((a, b) => a.title.localeCompare(b.title));\r\n1838:       }\r\n1839: \r\n1840:       return list;\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":2098,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:54:55Z","input_tokens":2151,"cache_read_tokens":108899,"output_tokens":8420,"thinking":"Initial focus is on refining the problem filtering mechanism. The current approach will be extended to incorporate a full-text search capability. This will allow for matching against multiple fields within each problem description, including title, LeetCode number, pattern, description, summary, and topic. The goal is to provide more flexible and comprehensive search functionality.\n\n\nImplemented full-text search across multiple problem description fields: title, LeetCode number, pattern, description, summary, and topic. The updated filtering logic combines full-text search with existing filters for topic, pattern, difficulty, and status. Current work focuses on refining the status filter to accurately reflect problem progress.\n\n\nRefining the status filter necessitates defining logic for \"attempted,\" \"not_started,\" \"review,\" \"bookmarked,\" and \"with_notes\" states, ensuring these are mutually exclusive where appropriate. Independently applied bookmark filter ensures bookmarked problems are always visible, regardless of other status filters.\n\nImplementing sorting options by title (ascending/descending), difficulty (ascending/descending), and learning order (ascending/descending) is the next step to enhance usability. The difficulty sort will use a rank assigned to each difficulty level to facilitate comparison.\n\n\nSorting logic is being implemented for the problem list. Sorting will include ascending and descending options for title, difficulty (using pre-defined difficulty ranks), and LeetCode number or ID as a fallback. Pagination logic is extracted to calculate the total number of pages and adjust the current page if it exceeds the calculated number of pages. Finally, the table metadata bar's content will be updated to accurately reflect the filtered and paginated problem data, including the total filtered count, the range of problems being displayed, and the total number of problems.\n\n\nThe table metadata bar will be updated to accurately display filtered problem counts, the displayed problem range, and the total number of problems. Pagination controls are only rendered if the page size is not \"all\" and there are multiple pages. Pagination logic incorporates ellipsis for condensed page number representation.\n\n\nPagination controls are being constructed to enable navigation through problem sets. Disabled states for navigation buttons are being implemented based on current page and total pages. Ellipsis is incorporated into page number display for condensed representation. The table metadata bar will dynamically reflect the filtered and paginated problem data.\n\n\nThe code suggests adding visual indicators for bookmarks, review status, and saved notes within the problem list. The presence of a \"Review\" badge, note indicator, or bookmark star will now signal the problem's status. The problem modal's route will be cleaned up on modal close.\n\n\nDirect routes to individual problems are being implemented using URL fragments to enable easy sharing. The modal will now include a route bar with a direct link and a copy button.\n\nBookmarking, review status, and solved state are integrated into the modal footer, including actions for toggling each state. The problem's route will be removed upon modal closure to maintain a clean URL. A copy route button and corresponding feedback mechanism are also incorporated.\n\n\nModal functionality is being added to allow for directly sharing problem routes via a URL fragment, including a copy-to-clipboard button with feedback. Review state toggle is integrated, and the route is cleaned up on modal close. The import modal is being implemented with appropriate header elements, including a title and close button. The modal's backdrop and card styling are being defined, with the intention of adding import functionality later.\n\n\nThe import modal requires parsing a JSON array of problem records.  Duplicate handling logic needs definition, offering \"skip\" (safe) and \"update\" options. The system will inspect specific problem fields for uniqueness during import.  Previewing the import and checking for duplicates will be implemented before execution.  Validation feedback and import execution are now disabled until preview is complete.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"# scratch/apply_phase4_part2.py\nimport os\n\nwith open('app_build/dsa_dashboard.js', 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    code = f.read()\n\n# 1. Add initRouter, importProblems, and showImportModal methods right before bindEvents or after formatTimeAgo\ntarget_helper_area = \"\"\"    formatTimeAgo(timestamp) {\n      if (!timestamp) return 'Recently';\"\"\"\n\nmethods_to_insert = \"\"\"    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // PHASE 4: URL HASH ROUTING & UNIQUE PROBLEM ROUTE\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    initRouter() {\n      if (typeof window === 'undefined') return;\n\n      const handleRouting = () => {\n        try {\n          const hash = window.location.hash || '';\n          if (!hash) return;\n\n          // Match #dsa/problem/:id or #problem/:id\n          const pMatch = hash.match(/^#(?:dsa\\\\/)?problem\\\\/(\\\\d+)/i);\n          if (pMatch) {\n            const id = parseInt(pMatch[1], 10);\n            if (this.problemsById && this.problemsById.has(id)) {\n              this.switchView('dsa');\n              if (typeof setTimeout === 'function') {\n                setTimeout(() => {\n                  this.showProblemModal(id);\n                }, 40);\n              } else {\n                this.showProblemModal(id);\n              }\n              return;\n            }\n          }\n\n          // Match #dsa/topic/:topic or #topic/:topic\n          const tMatch = hash.match(/^#(?:dsa\\\\/)?topic\\\\/(.+)/i);\n          if (tMatch) {\n            const decoded = decodeURIComponent(tMatch[1]).trim();\n            const matchedMeta = TOPIC_METADATA_30.find(m => m.name.toLowerCase() === decoded.toLowerCase());\n            if (matchedMeta) {\n              this.switchView('dsa');\n              this.openTopicDetailPage(matchedMeta.name);\n              return;\n            }\n          }\n\n          if (hash === '#dsa' || hash.startsWith('#dsa/')) {\n            this.switchView('dsa');\n          } else if (hash === '#visualizer') {\n            this.switchView('visualizer');\n          }\n        } catch (e) {\n          console.warn('Router error:', e);\n        }\n      };\n\n      if (typeof window.addEventListener === 'function') {\n        window.addEventListener('hashchange', handleRouting);\n      }\n      handleRouting();\n    }\n\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // PHASE 4: DUPLICATE PREVENTION & PROBLEM IMPORT ENGINE\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    importProblems(newProblems, options = { onDuplicate: 'skip' }) {\n      if (!Array.isArray(newProblems)) {\n        throw new Error('importProblems requires an array of problem objects');\n      }\n\n      const onDuplicate = options && options.onDuplicate === 'update' ? 'update' : 'skip';\n\n      const report = {\n        totalInput: newProblems.length,\n        imported: 0,\n        updated: 0,\n        skipped: 0,\n        duplicates: [],\n        errors: [],\n        totalCatalog: 0\n      };\n\n      const normalizeTitle = (t) => String(t || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '');\n      const normalizeUrl = (u) => String(u || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\\\\/+$/, '');\n\n      // Build lookup maps from current catalog for O(1) detection\n      const existingById = new Map();\n      const existingByLcNum = new Map();\n      const existingByNormTitle = new Map();\n      const existingByNormUrl = new Map();\n\n      this.problems.forEach(p => {\n        existingById.set(p.id, p);\n        if (p.leetcodeNumber) existingByLcNum.set(p.leetcodeNumber, p);\n        if (p.title) existingByNormTitle.set(normalizeTitle(p.title), p);\n        if (p.sourceUrl) existingByNormUrl.set(normalizeUrl(p.sourceUrl), p);\n      });\n\n      newProblems.forEach((raw, idx) => {\n        if (!raw || typeof raw !== 'object') {\n          report.errors.push({ index: idx, error: 'Invalid problem entry: not an object' });\n          return;\n        }\n\n        // Duplicate checks\n        let match = null;\n        let reason = null;\n\n        if (raw.id && existingById.has(raw.id)) {\n          match = existingById.get(raw.id);\n          reason = `Problem ID #${raw.id} already exists as '${match.title}'`;\n        } else if (raw.leetcodeNumber && existingByLcNum.has(raw.leetcodeNumber)) {\n          match = existingByLcNum.get(raw.leetcodeNumber);\n          reason = `LeetCode #${raw.leetcodeNumber} already exists as '${match.title}'`;\n        } else if (raw.title && existingByNormTitle.has(normalizeTitle(raw.title))) {\n          match = existingByNormTitle.get(normalizeTitle(raw.title));\n          reason = `Title '${raw.title}' duplicates existing '${match.title}'`;\n        } else if (raw.sourceUrl && existingByNormUrl.has(normalizeUrl(raw.sourceUrl))) {\n          match = existingByNormUrl.get(normalizeUrl(raw.sourceUrl));\n          reason = `Source URL duplicates existing '${match.title}'`;\n        }\n\n        if (match) {\n          report.duplicates.push({\n            inputIndex: idx,\n            candidateTitle: raw.title || `Entry #${idx + 1}`,\n            matchedId: match.id,\n            matchedTitle: match.title,\n            reason: reason\n          });\n\n          if (onDuplicate === 'update') {\n            if (raw.summary) match.summary = raw.summary;\n            if (raw.description) match.description = raw.description;\n            if (raw.pattern) match.pattern = raw.pattern;\n            if (Array.isArray(raw.examples) && raw.examples.length > 0) match.examples = raw.examples;\n            if (Array.isArray(raw.constraints) && raw.constraints.length > 0) match.constraints = raw.constraints;\n            if (Array.isArray(raw.prerequisites) && raw.prerequisites.length > 0) match.prerequisites = raw.prerequisites;\n            if (raw.referenceSolution) match.referenceSolution = raw.referenceSolution;\n            if (raw.starterCode) match.starterCode = raw.starterCode;\n            report.updated++;\n          } else {\n            report.skipped++;\n          }\n        } else {\n          // Assign clean collision-free unique ID\n          let newId = raw.id;\n          if (!newId || existingById.has(newId)) {\n            let maxId = this.problems.reduce((max, p) => Math.max(max, p.id || 0), 0);\n            newId = maxId + 1;\n          }\n\n          const validRecord = {\n            id: newId,\n            leetcodeNumber: raw.leetcodeNumber || newId,\n            title: String(raw.title || `Curated Problem #${newId}`).trim(),\n            sourceUrl: raw.sourceUrl || `https://leetcode.com/problems/${String(raw.title || '').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}/`,\n            difficulty: ['Easy', 'Medium', 'Hard'].includes(raw.difficulty) ? raw.difficulty : 'Medium',\n            primaryTopic: raw.primaryTopic || (Array.isArray(raw.topics) && raw.topics[0]) || 'Arrays',\n            topics: Array.isArray(raw.topics) && raw.topics.length > 0 ? raw.topics : [raw.primaryTopic || 'Arrays'],\n            topic: raw.topic || raw.primaryTopic || 'Arrays',\n            pattern: raw.pattern || 'Algorithmic Pattern',\n            description: raw.description || raw.summary || 'Problem description.',\n            summary: raw.summary || raw.description || 'Problem summary.',\n            examples: Array.isArray(raw.examples) ? raw.examples : [],\n            constraints: Array.isArray(raw.constraints) ? raw.constraints : [],\n            prerequisites: Array.isArray(raw.prerequisites) ? raw.prerequisites : [],\n            timeComplexity: raw.timeComplexity || 'O(n)',\n            spaceComplexity: raw.spaceComplexity || 'O(1)',\n            starterCode: raw.starterCode || raw.referenceSolution || '# Starter code\\\\n',\n            referenceSolution: raw.referenceSolution || raw.starterCode || '# Reference solution\\\\n',\n            verificationStatus: raw.verificationStatus || 'Community Curated'\n          };\n\n          this.problems.push(validRecord);\n          existingById.set(validRecord.id, validRecord);\n          if (validRecord.leetcodeNumber) existingByLcNum.set(validRecord.leetcodeNumber, validRecord);\n          existingByNormTitle.set(normalizeTitle(validRecord.title), validRecord);\n          existingByNormUrl.set(normalizeUrl(validRecord.sourceUrl), validRecord);\n          this.problemsById.set(validRecord.id, validRecord);\n          report.imported++;\n        }\n      });\n\n      report.totalCatalog = this.problems.length;\n      if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\n        window.DSA_PROBLEMS_LIBRARY = this.problems;\n      }\n      this.render();\n      return report;\n    }\n\n    showImportModal() {\n      const existing = document.getElementById('dsaImportModal');\n      if (existing && typeof existing.remove === 'function') existing.remove();\n\n      const modal = document.createElement('div');\n      modal.id = 'dsaImportModal';\n      modal.className = 'dsa-modal-backdrop';\n      modal.innerHTML = `\n        <div class=\"dsa-modal-card import-modal-card\">\n          <div class=\"dsa-modal-header\">\n            <div class=\"dsa-modal-title-row\">\n              <span class=\"lc-badge\">📥 Catalog Extension</span>\n              <h2 class=\"dsa-modal-title\">Import Additional DSA Problems</h2>\n            </div>\n            <button class=\"modal-close-btn\" id=\"btnImportModalClose\" title=\"Close import modal\">✕</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"dsa-modal-body\">\n            <p class=\"import-help-text\">\n              Paste a JSON array of problem records. The catalog automatically checks for duplicates by <strong>Problem ID</strong>, <strong>LeetCode Number</strong>, <strong>Title</strong>, and <strong>Source URL</strong> to preserve library integrity.\n            </p>\n            <div class=\"import-options-row\">\n              <span class=\"import-strategy-label\">Duplicate Policy:</span>\n              <label class=\"radio-label\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"dupStrategy\" value=\"skip\" checked> Skip Duplicates</label>\n              <label class=\"radio-label\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"dupStrategy\" value=\"update\"> Update Existing</label>\n              <button class=\"btn-import-sample\" id=\"btnPasteSampleJson\">📄 Load Sample</button>\n            </div>\n            <textarea id=\"importJsonTextarea\" class=\"import-json-textarea\" placeholder=\"[&#10;  {&#10;    \\\\\"title\\\\\": \\\\\"Subtree of Another Tree\\\\\",&#10;    \\\\\"leetcodeNumber\\\\\": 572,&#10;    \\\\\"difficulty\\\\\": \\\\\"Easy\\\\\",&#10;    \\\\\"primaryTopic\\\\\": \\\\\"Trees and Binary Trees\\\\\",&#10;    \\\\\"pattern\\\\\": \\\\\"Tree Matching\\\\\"&#10;  }&#10;]\"></textarea>\n            <div id=\"importValidationReport\" class=\"import-validation-box hidden\"></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"dsa-modal-footer\">\n            <div class=\"modal-footer-left\">\n              <button class=\"btn-hero-subtle\" id=\"btnPreviewImport\">🔍 Check for Duplicates</button>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"modal-footer-right\">\n              <button class=\"btn-hero-primary\" id=\"btnExecuteImport\" disabled>📥 Commit to Catalog</button>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      `;\n      document.body.appendChild(modal);\n\n      let parsedData = null;\n\n      modal.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n        if (e.target === modal || e.target.id === 'btnImportModalClose') {\n          modal.remove();\n        } else if (e.target.id === 'btnPasteSampleJson') {\n          const sample = [\n            {\n              title: \"Subtree of Another Tree\",\n              leetcodeNumber: 572,\n              difficulty: \"Easy\",\n              primaryTopic: \"Trees and Binary Trees\",\n              pattern: \"Tree Traversal DFS\",\n              summary: \"Given roots of two binary trees, determine if tree subRoot has identical structure and values to a subtree of root.\"\n            },\n            {\n              title: \"Two Sum\",\n              leetcodeNumber: 1,\n              difficulty: \"Easy\",\n              primaryTopic: \"Arrays\",\n              pattern: \"Hash Map Complement\",\n              summary: \"Duplicate problem test - should be flagged as duplicate.\"\n            }\n          ];\n          const ta = modal.querySelector('#importJsonTextarea');\n          if (ta) ta.value = JSON.stringify(sample, null, 2);\n        } else if (e.target.id === 'btnPreviewImport') {\n          const ta = modal.querySelector('#importJsonTextarea');\n          const reportBox = modal.querySelector('#importValidationReport');\n          const execBtn = modal.querySelector('#btnExecuteImport');\n          if (!ta || !reportBox) return;\n\n          try {\n            parsedData = JSON.parse(ta.value.trim());\n            if (!Array.isArray(parsedData)) parsedData = [parsedData];\n\n            // Dry-run check duplicates without mutating\n            let dups = [];\n            let validNew = 0;\n            const normalize = (t) => String(t || '').trim().toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '');\n\n            parsedData.forEach((item, i) => {\n              const matched = this.problems.find(p => \n                (item.id && p.id === item.id) ||\n                (item.leetcodeNumber && p.leetcodeNumber === item.leetcodeNumber) ||\n                (item.title && normalize(p.title) === normalize(item.title))\n              );\n              if (matched) {\n                dups.push(`'${item.title || 'Entry #' + (i+1)}' matches existing LC #${matched.leetcodeNumber} (${matched.title})`);\n              } else {\n                validNew++;\n              }\n            });\n\n            reportBox.classList.remove('hidden');\n            reportBox.innerHTML = `\n              <div class=\"report-summary\">\n                <strong>Analysis Result:</strong> ${parsedData.length} problems analyzed.\n                <div class=\"report-line report-valid\">✓ <strong>${validNew}</strong> new unique problem(s) ready to import.</div>\n                ${dups.length > 0 ? `<div class=\"report-line report-dup\">⚠️ <strong>${dups.length}</strong> duplicate(s) detected:</div><ul class=\"dup-list\">${dups.map(d => '<li>' + this.escapeHTML(d) + '</li>').join('')}</ul>` : ''}\n              </div>\n            `;\n            if (execBtn) execBtn.disabled = (validNew === 0 && dups.length === 0);\n          } catch (err) {\n            reportBox.classList.remove('hidden');\n            reportBox.innerHTML = `<div class=\"report-error\">❌ JSON Parsing Error: ${this.escapeHTML(err.message)}</div>`;\n            if (execBtn) execBtn.disabled = true;\n          }\n        } else if (e.target.id === 'btnExecuteImport') {\n          if (!parsedData) return;\n          const strat = modal.querySelector('input[name=\"dupStrategy\"]:checked')?.value || 'skip';\n          const report = this.importProblems(parsedData, { onDuplicate: strat });\n          modal.remove();\n          alert(`Import Complete!\\n\\nImported: ${report.imported}\\nUpdated: ${report.updated}\\nDuplicates Skipped: ${report.skipped}\\nTotal Catalog: ${report.totalCatalog}`);\n        }\n      });\n    }\n\n    formatTimeAgo(timestamp) {\"\"\"\n\nassert target_helper_area in code, \"target_helper_area not found\"\ncode = code.replace(target_helper_area, methods_to_insert, 1)\n\nprint(\"Part 2 (initRouter, importProblems, showImportModal) added successfully\")\n\nwith open('app_build/dsa_dashboard.js.tmp', 'w', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write(code)\n\nos.replace('app_build/dsa_dashboard.js.tmp', 'app_build/dsa_dashboard.js')\nprint(\"Part 2 file replaced successfully\")\n","Description":"Apply Part 2 to dsa_dashboard.js","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef\\scratch\\apply_phase4_part2.py","toolAction":"Creating apply_phase4_part2.py","toolSummary":"Create apply script part 2"}}]}
